course: dictionary
lesson: 8506
title: Reading abbreviations
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer name. SARS is an abbreviation, and its letters stand for words: Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome. Context helps you check what it means. «COVID-19 is caused by the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus, first found in 2019, which is where the 19 comes from, and in most children it is mild.» Here the word is part of a virus name, not just the illness.
explain: The same letters can mean different things in different places. SAR can mean a Special Administrative Region of China, as Hong Kong and Macau are. So when you meet an abbreviation, ask: what is the topic? In a science lesson, SARS is a lung illness, but in a geography lesson it may point to a place.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. Does «SARS-CoV-2 causes COVID-19» still make sense? Yes, so the virus is the cause and COVID-19 is the illness it causes.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a word or name.
fact: «SARS» stands for Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome, a serious lung illness.
fact: SARS spread to several countries in 2002–2003.
fact: «SARS-CoV-2» is the name of the virus that causes COVID-19.
fact: «SAR» can mean a Special Administrative Region, such as Hong Kong or Macau.
exercise: In «COVID-19 is caused by the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus, first found in 2019», what is the name of the virus? | Hong Kong | 2019 | COVID-19 | *SARS-CoV-2
exercise: What does the abbreviation SARS stand for? | Simple Animal Research Study | *Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome | Special Administrative Region Syndrome
exercise: In Hong Kong, what can SAR mean? | *A Special Administrative Region of China | A grey, wet day | A petrol station | A kind of lung
test: Why was the virus named SARS-CoV-2? | Because it is a petrol station code | Because it has the number 19 in its name | *Because it is related to the virus that caused SARS | Because it was first found on a farm
test: Which illness was a serious lung illness that spread to several countries in 2002–2003? | Servo | Dreich | *SARS | COVID-19
exam: In «in most children it is mild», what does mild mean? | Very loud | *Not very serious | Very old | Very cold
